lance during one part of the dance. he managed the earlier steps, then always put a foot down. his teacher suggested short practice periods instead of one exhausting afternoon. each day, luca held the difficult position for a little longer. he marked his progress, including days when he wobbled again. after several weeks, he could hold the pose throughout the music. the rest of the dance had not become easier by itself. he had spent time on the part that needed repeated work.","lucas helped put the food shopping away. the eggs sat above some heavy cans. he lifted the eggs out with both hands. he wanted to keep them safe from breaking. then he put the cans on the shelf.","lunch,","luz shared bean seeds with her nearby neighbours. their gardens soon held strong new shoots. snails later ate luz''s own young plants. they brought spare shoots, and her garden grew again.","made its surface wet","made the model bridge bend","mae lent spare mittens to a classmate whose hands were cold. when mae later broke her arm, the classmate offered to carry her books without being asked. mae realized that the care she had shown was now coming back in a different way.","magnifier","maids","making a shared place easier to use","making every part exactly the same size","mara began explaining her idea for the model. her partner interrupted again and moved her pieces aside. mara pressed her lips together and said firmly, “please let me finish. i have listened to your idea.” she kept her own plan open on the table.","mara had rehearsed her song all week. now she stood behind the curtain, twisting the edge of her sleeve. when her name was called, she took a deep breath and checked the opening words again before stepping forward.","mara needed a bag for a walk where rain was forecast. one bag had bright beads and colours that matched her coat. its thin straps strained when she added her lunch and spare clothes. a plain bag had strong straps and a cover that shut tightly. mara tested both with the same things inside before deciding. she chose the plain one, though she still liked the other''s pattern. rain fell during the walk, but her clothes stayed dry. she opened the bag at the shelter without needing to replace anything.","mara put cups out for the class picnic. twenty children needed drinks. at first, she put out eighteen cups. her friend saw that two children needed cups. mara added two more before lunch began.","mara put on her goggles. swimmers splashed along marked lanes under a high roof. a coach blew a whistle from the edge. mara climbed down the ladder into the water.","marisol got off the bus one stop before her intended destination. rain began while she checked how far she would need to walk. a small museum nearby offered somewhere dry until the shower passed. she expected to wait near the entrance without looking around. a display of old ship models caught her attention instead. she asked the guide about a tiny boat from her grandparents'' town. the rain stopped, but she stayed until the tour had finished. next week, she returned deliberately with questions for the same guide.","marta placed her recorder in its blue case before going upstairs. the next morning, she heard uneven notes from her brother''s room. he had been practising finger movements without an instrument yesterday. marta hurried to school with the blue case in her bag. when music began, she opened it and found only the cloth. her teacher said no instruments had been collected that morning. at home, her brother stopped practising when she asked about it. his new sheet of recorder music lay on his desk.","may came home from a muddy walk. she left her boots on the porch. then she went inside in her socks. dad put a mat beside the boots to catch the drops of water.","maya planted sunflower seeds in a small pot. she added a label with her name. then she watered the dry soil. she put the pot on the sunny windowsill. a green shoot appeared there on friday.","maya tried to join the same pieces five times. each time, her small model fell apart. she sighed loudly and pushed the pieces away. her forehead wrinkled as she stared at the pile.","maya watched the moon from the same window each evening. she drew its shape beside that day''s date. on cloudy evenings, she marked the box hidden instead. at first, each drawing seemed like a separate little picture. after four weeks, she laid the pages in a row. the bright shape grew wider, then became narrow again. her cousin could see that pattern without watching every night. her cousin pointed to matching shapes several pages apart.","measure a cup of oats for the bowl","medals were polished","meeting","mei walked between rows of living plants in pots. labels explained how much light each plant needed. a worker helped her choose one that suited a sunny window and added a bag of potting soil. mei paid for it at a counter near stacks of empty flowerpots.","mia offered to teach a new club member how chess works. he said he had watched games but never joined this club. mia opened the box and began looking for the instruction sheet. before she found it, he placed every piece correctly. he explained which moves would leave mia''s king in danger. when she moved a bishop wrongly, he described its allowed path. the board stood on a small table beneath the clock. other players nearby were still choosing partners for their first game.","mia stopped her brother entering the garden den after they argued. her collection stayed untouched, and every cushion remained where she put it. however, the pretend shop was dull when she played both customers herself. her brother missed their game but disliked being blamed for every mess. they agreed that special models needed permission before anyone moved them. other toys could still be used together and put away afterwards. mia opened the den again without removing every rule. two customers soon waited at the shop while the models stayed safe.","mid","midnight","mika filled a plant pot right to the rim with soil. when she watered it, muddy water spilled over the edge. she removed some soil and left room for the water to soak in. when potting another plant, she remembered to leave the same useful space at the top.","mika wanted to take the class photograph without accepting any advice. in her first picture, faces disappeared in shadows beside the window. she tried again from the same place and got the same result. a neighbour who enjoyed photography offered to explain the light. mika finally listened and moved so the window lit the children''s faces. she checked the new picture before asking everyone to smile again. the finished photograph clearly showed each child in the group. mika wrote the neighbour''s helpful lighting tip beside her own picture notes.","mika’s simple wooden flute made a weak, rough sound. a small piece of paper was stuck across the opening where air passed. her teacher carefully removed it. mika blew in the same way as before, and a clear note sounded. the flute had not been replaced.","miles and grandpa raked leaves from the path. the wind kept blowing them across the garden. grandpa held a large bag open. miles pushed the loose leaves into it. they tied it shut before more wind came.","milly carried ice cream on a warm walk. the heat softened it until it started dripping. she licked fast to catch the drops. white drops still ran down onto her fingers.","milo disliked the dark corner beside his bed at night. dad listened instead of laughing and left a torch within reach. at first, milo checked every shadow before settling under his blanket. dad reminded him that he could call whenever he needed help. after several nights, milo left the torch beside the pillow unused. he still knew where it was and could reach it easily. one night, dad found him sleeping with the room completely dark. the torch remained ready on the bedside shelf the next morning.","milo guessed how much string his model needed and cut it too short. instead of throwing the model away, he measured each side, joined a fresh length and tried again. on the next model he measured before cutting.","milo''s tooth had wobbled for a week. he wiggled it at breakfast and at bath time. he laughed at dinner, and the tooth popped out. he caught it in his hand. milo put it under his pillow that night.","min gave the fish extra food every day. uneaten bits made the tank''s clear water cloudy. an adult helped min measure the right amount. with less waste, the clean water stayed clear again.","mina opened a box from her old friend. inside was the scarf she had lost. she pressed it to her cheek and smiled. then she hurried to get a thank-you card. she kept the scarf beside her all evening.","mina''s kitten often slipped behind furniture without making any noise. its grey fur was difficult to see in the dark gaps. once, mina searched several rooms before finding it behind the sofa. her mother fitted a light bell to its safe cat collar. later, mina heard a jingle beneath the armchair before seeing anything. she knelt beside that chair instead of checking every room. the kitten came out when she called, just as it usually did. mina left the other furniture alone and fetched its dinner.","mina’s large jigsaw seemed impossible on the first evening. she sorted the pieces by edges and colours and worked on a little section after school. some sections took many attempts. over two weeks the empty spaces shrank, until she placed the final piece and saw the complete picture.","mind","minute","mira usually watered the class plant. on friday she was absent, so ben asked lila to do the job. lila filled the jug and watered the dry soil. ben wiped up the water that spilled on the table.","missing","mixed with a quick stir","mo left his bike outside without shelter all winter. rain kept wetting the bare metal. the wet metal slowly grew orange rust. by spring, the chain was stiff and rusty.","mo wanted to remember a long message for assembly. he learned one short part each day. then he practiced joining the parts together. at assembly, he remembered the whole message.","mock-foundation-word:bar","mock-foundation-word:belt","mock-foundation-word:bench","mock-foundation-word:bin","mock-foundation-word:born","mock-foundation-word:broom","mock-foundation-word:brown","mock-foundation-word:bug","mock-foundation-word:burst","mock-foundation-word:car","mock-foundation-word:clap","mock-foundation-word:claw","mock-foundation-word:click","mock-foundation-word:clown","mock-foundation-word:cord","mock-foundation-word:crow","mock-foundation-word:crown","mock-foundation-word:cup","mock-foundation-word:curl","mock-foundation-word:dirt","mock-foundation-word:dog","mock-foundation-word:drum","mock-foundation-word:fern","mock-foundation-word:flow","mock-foundation-word:hen","mock-foundation-word:herd","mock-foundation-word:jar","mock-foundation-word:joint","mock-foundation-word:jug","mock-foundation-word:leg","mock-foundation-word:list","mock-foundation-word:loft","mock-foundation-word:milk","mock-foundation-word:mist","mock-foundation-word:mud","mock-foundation-word:pan","mock-foundation-word:plug","mock-foundation-word:plum","mock-foundation-word:port","mock-foundation-word:pot","mock-foundation-word:purse","mock-foundation-word:sand","mock-foundation-word:serve","mock-foundation-word:sort","mock-foundation-word:spot","mock-foundation-word:stamp","mock-foundation-word:star","mock-foundation-word:stern","mock-foundation-word:stomp","mock-foundation-word:stool","mock-foundation-word:surf","mock-foundation-word:tar","mock-foundation-word:ten","mock-foundation-word:tent","mock-foundation-word:term","mock-foundation-word:trip","mock-foundation-word:truck","mock-foundation-word:turn","mock.capacity.cause_effect.basket-handle","mock.capacity.cause_effect.blocked-flute","mock.capacity.cause_effect.bottle-squeeze","mock.capacity.cause_effect.bus-delay","mock.capacity.cause_effect.cake-light","mock.capacity.cause_effect.cardboard-wet"