uring the quiet reading lesson. bangs, voices and loud squawks mixed into a sudden uproar. children turned towards the windows while a teacher went to investigate. a delivery box had fallen beside a group of startled geese. the birds flapped around as two adults moved the scattered boxes. one person called directions over the noise of the others. after the geese settled and the boxes were stacked, calm returned. the children could hear their teacher reading softly once more.","a contest between players or teams","a cover on a container","a crow ignored the scarecrow until the farmer clapped and the dog barked.","a curled piece of metal that pushes back","a cyclist lent a helmet to a skater. she wore it. the skater fastened the helmet strap under her own chin.","a delivery driver needs to know where to leave a parcel after the office closes.","a draft, or first version of a piece of writing, lay on mina’s desk. she crossed out one sentence and added a better ending. her final copy would come later. the open window moved the paper, but did not change the words.","a drawing can fade in strong sunlight. damp can damage its paper, and rough handling can tear an edge. a protective frame, a dry place and careful handling reduce these problems. keeping artwork safe involves more than choosing where it looks attractive.","a drink spilled over a book with a wipe-clean cover. the cover became wet, but the pages beneath stayed dry. a matching uncovered booklet beside it had wet pages. both books had pictures on their first pages.","a duck dived into the pond. splash! water flew over the stones.","a duck rests by the pond___","a duck spreads oil over its feathers. rain runs off the oily surface. dry feathers trap warm air next to its body.","a duck swims quietly.","a faint light glowed at the far end of the tunnel.","a feather drifts beside the wall, it turns and twirls before its fall. the bird has gone beyond my view, its tiny gift still holds the blue.","a fish uses gills to 