e","struck","strut matches the complete spoken target. street and straight keep the consonant sounds but change the vowel.","stub","stuck matches the complete spoken target. stick and stack keep the consonant sounds but change the vowel.","summer at the lake by rosa park and dev stone illustrated by clara moss","sun does not share the complete vowel-and-ending sequence of the rhyming pair.","sun flower","sun matches the complete spoken target. sin and sane keep the consonant sounds but change the vowel.","sunk drops or changes a consonant in the target cluster, or keeps the cluster but changes the rest of skunk.","sunk","sunlight had drained the curtain’s color; it looked ___.","surfboard","suri’s cup tipped during the quiet meeting. her cheeks grew hot, and she looked down instead of meeting anyone’s eyes. a friend passed her a cloth from the table.","surprise-visit","sweet fruit scented the stall. bright cloth shaded the baskets, and a seller called prices above the rumble of passing carts.","swerve","swift things passed the window of our slow train. a motorbike sped along the nearby road. a hawk rushed past after a small bird. another train vanished before we could count its carriages.","swim across the pond","swim is not the word at the requested position or the word with the missing capital.","swimming lessons at our school start after lunch every friday.","swing-push","t is the lowercase form of T, a different letter.","tHE","tHe","tHey","tUesday","tab","tail and small","take animals home","tall, taller, tallest written by luis park and eve day pictures by kim lane","tame","tara felt drowsy during her favourite evening show. drowsy means so sleepy you can hardly stay awake. her eyes kept closing before the story ended. she rested her head on a soft cushion.","taste","tea is grown in parts of ___.","team has a different vowel from the requested sound.","team-invitation","telescope-night","tell a friend that your class planted a tree.","tell borrowers to return books to the desk, not directly to the shelves.","tell dad that you swam without arm bands today.","tell families bus 4 is late, while buses 2 and 3 are on time.","tell families that the trip is now on tuesday, not monday. the place is unchanged.","tell families the concert is moving to the hall but will still start at six.","tell gran that an egg hatched in your classroom.","tell people to put empty bottles in the marked box.","tell pupils soup has replaced rice today. fruit is still being served.","tell readers where to put books they have finished with.","tell someone that your missing bag is green.","tell visitors to look at the old pots but not touch them.","tell walkers to use the small bridge because the large bridge is closed.","tell walkers to wait at the crossing until the helper signals.","tell your class that the eggs have hatched.","tell your cousin that snow fell at your home.","tell your family that a new library has opened.","tell your friend that you have a new puppy.","tell your friend that your class has a new fish.","tell your friend that your first tooth fell out.","tell your teacher that your cousins are visiting.","tent-rope","tess frowned and stamped her foot when the game pieces fell. the board lay on the rug.","test matches the complete spoken target. taste and toast keep the consonant sounds but change the vowel.","text a: a pet rabbit needs fresh drinking water each day. it also needs space to move and suitable food. text b: a pet guinea pig needs fresh drinking water each day. a quiet hiding place can help it feel safe.","text a: a tortoise has a hard shell that helps protect its soft body. when threatened, it can pull parts of its body inside. text b: a hedgehog’s sharp spines help protect it. curling up presents those spines towards a threat.","text a: after painting, our group washed brushes, closed paint pots and cleared the table. then we displayed the pictures. text b: after building, the club sorted tools, returned spare pieces and swept the floor. then everyone went home.","text a: bean plants need light and water. text b: sunflowers need water and have tall stems.","text a: ducks have feathers and lay eggs. text b: hens lay eggs and scratch the ground for food.","text a: evan flipped the pancake and caught it neatly in the pan. text b: i flipped the pancake, and i was pleased when it landed in my pan.","text a: i climbed the hill and waved. text b: kim climbed the hill and waved.","text a: i held the branch while my friend tied it to our shelter. text b: tia held the branch while her friend tied it to their shelter.","text a: i still remember my first day on the farm. i was afraid to feed the calves. text b: lily remembered her first day on the farm, when she was afraid to feed the calves.","text a: luca heard rain on the tent and pulled his blanket close. text b: rain drummed above me. i pulled my blanket close and listened.","text a: our bus followed a fixed route and stopped to collect passengers. the driver steered while we sat together. text b: i cycled to school with dad. we chose the quiet streets and stopped when we needed a rest.","text a: our library lends books and provides tables where visitors can study. staff help people find what they need. text b: the mobile library lends books from a van. it visits villages that are far from a library building.","text a: our team crowded around the notice. we had won the photo competition! text b: the team crowded around the notice and discovered that it had won the photo competition.","text a: the hikers slept in a fabric tent that folded into a bag. they carried it to the next campsite. text b: the stone shelter stayed beside the mountain path. travellers could rest there, but could not take it away.","text a: the market was quiet before sunrise. sellers arranged fruit while only a few early shoppers passed. text b: by late morning, the same market was crowded. shoppers queued and sellers called across the busy stalls.","text a: the sailors hauled the small boat onto the beach before the waves grew higher. text b: we hauled our boat onto the beach just before the next wave reached us.","text a: we covered young plants with a mesh frame to keep birds from eating the leaves. rain could pass through the mesh. text b: the gardener used shiny hanging strips to discourage birds from landing among the seedlings.","text a: we pushed our boat into the water. text b: the children pushed their boat into the water.","text a: we walked through the museum together and stopped at the giant skeleton. text b: the class walked through the museum and stopped at the giant skeleton.","text a: “i cannot reach,” said zed, stretching towards the shelf. text b: i stretched towards the shelf but could not reach the book.","thank a friend for practising lines with you, rather than for making the costume.","thank a friend for sharing a book. tell them which part you enjoyed.","thank a visitor who brought maps and explained how to use them.","thank amir for lending his bike and say when you will return it.","thank ana for helping find your dog. the dog was not a gift.","thank the bus driver for waiting while your teacher counted the class.","thank the caretaker for adding a ramp so your trolley can enter.","thank the cooks for preparing lunch and the helpers for serving it.","thank your brother for returning your missing glove. do not claim he bought it.","thank your neighbour for saving your seedlings from the cold and say they are growing.","that hurt___","that soup is ___ hot to eat!","that swing is ___ special spot.","the ___ animal was bigger than the rest.","the ___ blanket felt gentle on my cheek.","the ___ box weighed more than i could lift.","the ___ button was smaller than my fingernail.","the ___ checked the patient’s temperature before giving the medicine.","the ___ checks out books and helps readers find them.","the ___ curled into a ball with its sharp spines pointing out.","the ___ curled its tail around sea grass underwater.","the ___ dancer thanked the crowd.","the ___ displayed old tools with labels about their history.","the ___ dripped on the rug.","the ___ flew high in the wind.","the ___ flicked its bushy tail and carried a nut up the tree.","the ___ from dinner included plates and bowls.","the ___ giggled in their cribs.","the ___ gripped the rock with eight arms.","the ___ had black-and-white stripes.","the ___ helped the sick dog.","the ___ helped us find a book and recorded its return date.","the ___ hooted all night long.","the ___ kitten slept through the storm.","the ___ knife went through the pumpkin easily.","the ___ lit the sky at dawn.","the ___ measured wood before building a cupboard.","the ___ played music with two sticks.","the ___ pond was too far down for my feet to reach the bottom.","the ___ repaired a hole in my tooth.","the ___ river flows north.","the ___ sailed into the bay.","the ___ sang to the crowd.","the ___ sat on the throne.","the ___ sea tossed the little boat.","the ___ sheet let us see every detail behind it.","the ___ showed that the water was too hot for the fish.","the ___ snapped under the nest.","the ___ soup burned my lip.","the ___ spun silk around its body to make a cocoon.","the ___ stone stayed firm when squeezed.","the ___ stopped the match after a foul.","the ___ tapped holes in the trunk with its beak.","the ___ towel dripped onto the floor.","the ___ tree rose above every roof.","the ___ wood scratched my hand with splinters.","the ___ wore a golden crown.","the alarm sounded after everyone had sat down, just before the film was due to start.","the ancient tower has stood for hundreds of years.","the animals found shelters during the storm. a rabbit stayed in its burrow. birds huddled inside a hollow tree. even a beetle hid under a curled leaf, out of the driving rain.","the athlete can ___ fifty laps a day.","the atlas shows where ___ is.","the baby ___ climbed into its mother’s pouch.","the baby crawls slowly.","the baby was asleep, so i ___ past the door.","the baby was asleep, so we chose to ___ instead of speaking loudly.","the baby was sleeping, so dad ___ the door gently.","the bag belongs to a girl called joy.","the bag broke. tell the reader why.","the bag was heavy to carry. this bag feels ___.","the baked crust shone yellow-brown; it looked ___.","the baker checked that the kitchen was spotless before work began. the counters were perfectly clean, with no crumbs or sticky marks. boxes were still stacked beside the door, waiting to be unpacked. although that corner looked crowded, every surface had been carefully washed. when flour spilled during mixing, the baker wiped it up immediately. she checked beneath the bowl rather than cleaning only visible patches. at closing time, the room was not empty of equipment. the equipment and work areas were simply clean again throughout.","the baker lent her rolling pin to the cook.","the baker mixed ground wheat ___ with water to make dough.","the baker sliced two ___ of bread.","the ball hit the vase. it broke. the vase broke.","the ball hit the window. it cracked. the ball stayed round, but the glass had a split.","the ball was wedged between two thick roots. jo pulled, but it would not move. she tried from the other side of the tree. it still stayed firmly in that narrow gap. an adult helped her loosen it gently.","the basket held three fuzzy ___.","the basket was empty; ___ apples remained.","the bat flew out of the cave. glossary bat: a flying animal bat: a stick used to hit a ball","the beach has sand. crabs live there. everyone should visit this lovely beach.","the beam was low, so i had to ___ my head.","the bean","the bed felt ___ after our long walk.","the bee landed on a ___ and gathered nectar.","the bell usually rings at nine, but yesterday it ___ at ten.","the bench is made of ___ from the old oak.","the bench still had wet paint, so a sign warned people against sitting there.","the bench under the tree stayed cool at noon. a sunny bench nearby felt hot. birds sat in the tree.","the big bell went clang! birds flew from the roof.","the bird rested on a ledge, a narrow flat shelf of rock sticking out from the cliff. there was just enough space for its feet. the cliff dropped steeply below it.","the birds on the roof ___ singing now.","the block tower fell during our test. explain why.","the blue paint was almost black; it was ___ blue.","the blue umbrella written and drawn by iris lake printed by field books","the board stayed straight when i tried to bend it; it was ___.","the boards were brown. they creaked under my feet.","the boat follows the river through egypt.","the boats rock gently in a row, their lanterns make the water glow. a rope taps softly on the quay, while darkness settles on the sea.","the book on the highest shelf belongs to our teacher___","the book showed animals in their habitats. a frog sat in a pond, a camel walked across a desert and a squirrel climbed a forest tree. each animal was shown where it normally lived.","the book you want has a train on its cover.","the book","the bookmark is between pages 24 and 25. you have already read page 24.","the books under my coat ___ to the library.","the boot went deep into soft mud under the child’s weight.","the bowls were beside the jug. we put ___ into the cupboard, but left the jug out.","the box held keepsakes from our seaside trip. there was a ticket, postcard, and tiny shell. each object helped us remember a special day. we showed them while telling friends about our holiday.","the box of coloured pencils ___ on the shelf now.","the box of costumes belongs to ___.","the boy loosened the knot and opened his parcel.","the boys have a ball. ___ play outside.","the boys watched their sister perform. ___ clapped when she finished.","the brass trumpet gleamed. a loud note filled the hall.","the bridge test must happen only when the glue is dry. test the bridge ___ the glue is completely dry.","the broom woke up and swept the room by itself. dust gathered beside the chair.","the burst bag sent seeds in many different directions. the seeds ___ across the floor.","the bus arrived while we were counting the trees___","the bus arrived. we climbed aboard. dad waved. away we went!","the bus could not continue along the lane. explain why.","the bus stopped so three ___ could get off.","the bus stops right ___, where i am standing.","the bus to windermere leaves after lunch.","the busy nest author: leo hart illustrator: imani day","the buzzing ___ gathered nectar from a flower.","the café serves three kinds of soup today. jo says tomato soup tastes best. arun thinks soup is a much more enjoyable lunch than sandwiches.","the cake bakes for sixty minutes: one ___.","the cake cooled we added the icing","the canceled trip had been my hope all week; i felt ___.","the captain said these words: everyone is on board.","the card contained good ___ for the coming year.","the card shows 8. write the number word: ___.","the carpenter cut a plank from solid ___.","the carpenter fitted two ___ for our books.","the carpenter sanded a rough piece of ___.","the chef laid five ___ by the plates.","the child said these words: may i borrow a ruler?","the child went up the rope by pulling with both hands and pushing with both feet.","the children beside the teacher ___ ready now.","the children gave their teacher some flowers, and she placed them beside the classroom window.","the children must wait outside the locked gate until an adult opens it for them.","the children washed clay from their hands in a basin, a wide bowl that held warm water. they dipped their fingers below the surface and rubbed off the mud.","the children will meet after lunch, although their teacher arrives before lunch.","the choir practices in the hall every tuesday.","the class counted vehicles passing the school. a bus stopped, two bicycles rolled past and a delivery van turned the corner. each carried someone or something along the road.","the class found a vacant bird box near the playground. it was empty; no nest or bird was inside it. the entrance had become blocked with a dry leaf. an adult cleared the opening and checked the wooden sides. the children stood well back while the box was inspected. they hoped a pair of birds might use it in spring. a sign reminded everyone to keep the area quiet. the box stayed in its tree, ready for a future visitor.","the class had planned an outdoor concert, but rain began before the visitors arrived. noor suggested moving the chairs into the hall. everyone helped, and the music started indoors just in time.","the class has arrived at the farm. the return trip has not started.","the class helps keep our playground tidy.","the class prepared carefully for the visitors.","the class tested two fabric roofs above matching model shelters. the first roof was permeable when water was poured over it. tiny drops passed through spaces in the cloth and reached the floor. the second roof kept its floor dry during the same test. both materials bent easily and supported the same small wooden weight. the class placed paper underneath to record where the drops landed. after drying both models, they repeated the test with fresh paper. wet marks appeared beneath the first roof again, in several places.","the class trip is in june.","the classroom bell could not be heard in the playground. a larger speaker was fitted facing the yard. after testing its volume, staff could make announcements that everyone outside could hear.","the classroom held twenty ___ and one teacher.","the climb towards the lookout was steeper than the family expected. they stopped twice to rest and wondered whether to turn back. at the top, a wide view of the valley repaid their effort. they could see the winding river and farms beyond the distant trees. nobody exchanged money, and the lookout had no ticket office. the tired walkers stayed much longer than they had planned. on the way down, they described their favourite parts of the view. each agreed that reaching the top had been worth the climb.","the climbers could see everest from their camp.","the climbing frame is repaired, but the slide is still closed.","the clock struck ___ times at that hour.","the clock struck six as ravi dropped his cup. he whispered a spell to the clock. its hands spun backwards, the pieces joined together, and the cup jumped safely into his hand.","the cloth was a vivid, bright red called ___.","the cloth was absorbent; it soaked up spilled water. the wet patch became smaller as we wiped. soon, the table was dry and the cloth heavy. we squeezed the water out over the sink.","the club is full this week but has places next week.","the coach asked whether i had brought my hat.","the coach called my sister and me. she wanted to speak to ___.","the coat has a smooth blue outer layer. water forms drops on that layer and rolls away without soaking through. there are two deep pockets, and a yellow loop lets the coat hang on a hook.","the coat kept me dry but did not keep me warm. i stayed dry, ___ i still felt cold.","the coin fell from my hand and ___ across the floor on its edge.","the comb lost several ___ when it snapped.","the concert begins at six o’clock. dad says evening concerts are always the best. i think the flute is a nicer instrument than the trumpet.","the cook chopped carrots. the helper peeled potatoes.","the cook needs to know how many children will eat lunch today.","the cook peeled five ___ for the soup.","the costume sleeve was too long. we pinned it safely, measured again and shortened it. it now fitted without dragging.","the count went seven, ___, nine.","the cup is empty___","the cups are clean. ___ are on the shelf.","the curtains opened and actors stepped onto the stage of the ___.","the cyclist got off at the steep hill and pushed the bicycle to the top.","the dancer can ___ across the stage.","the dentist counted twenty baby ___ in my mouth.","the dentist gave milo a sticker for sitting calmly.","the desert plant has thick stems that store water. a waxy coating reduces water loss. its flowers open in bright colours, and insects visit them.","the desert stretched beyond what we could see; it was ___.","the diary says our visitors arrive in february.","the dinosaur room will close for repairs from monday to friday. the rest of the museum will remain open. visitors can see a small display of fossils in the entrance hall during the repair work.","the display model is made of wood. the guide thinks it is the finest model in the room. i find its tiny windows delightful.","the display showed different fasteners. a button held a shirt closed, a zip joined the sides of a bag and a buckle secured a belt. all kept things joined or shut.","the dog belongs to ella.","the dog can ___ in the soil.","the dog wore a soft collar. its metal tags jingled.","the dogs play outside.","the dogs run home.","the door creaked. a shadow slid across the room. a clock ticked steadily beside an open book.","the door swung on a ___ fixed to the frame.","the doorbell rang we opened the door","the drama class practised speaking across the large school hall. ade spoke clearly, sending each word towards the children at the back. bola began to mutter when her turn arrived. her low, unclear words barely reached the person standing beside her. the teacher could not tell whether she was repeating the right sentence. she asked bola to lift her head and speak more openly. this time, the words reached the other end of the room. the script itself had not changed between bola''s two attempts.","the driver rang the bell before the passenger lifted her suitcase from the rack.","the driver said these words: please take a seat.","the dry biscuit broke into many loose bits; it was ___.","the dry twig snapped with a light touch because it was ___.","the ducks swim in the pond.","the edge of land beside water","the empty basket felt as light as a feather when ana lifted it from the shelf.","the empty basket was light enough for the small child to carry. glossary light: not heavy light: brightness that lets you see dark: having little brightness","the empty bottle rolled away.","the empty flowerpot stood near the gate.","the end of the two strings ___ tied to a hook.","the evening show began with quiet music beside the dark lake. then a dazzling burst of white fireworks spread above the water. its brilliant light made the far bank visible for a moment. people blinked and shaded their eyes before looking up again. the coloured bursts afterwards were beautiful but much less bright. even the lamps along the path seemed dull during the display. sam could hear the bangs, but he kept watching the light. he described its brightness when drawing the scene the next morning.","the fallen apple rolled down the hill.","the fallen boxes caused a jam in the narrow passage. glossary jam: a sweet fruit spread jam: a blockage that stops movement lid: a cover on a container","the family has changed how it uses water. they fixed the dripping bathroom tap. their bathroom has yellow tiles. they collect rain in a barrel for watering plants. their garden path curves around an apple tree.","the farmer inspected a fragile shell left beside the henhouse. it was delicate and could break under even gentle pressure. she placed it in a shallow dish lined with cotton. the children looked closely without passing it from hand to hand. a small opening showed where the chick had pushed through. they drew the shell and marked the opening on their pictures. afterwards, the teacher carried the dish back to the classroom. everyone moved slowly to keep their find in one piece.","the father held his baby ___ gently.","the feeder hangs high above the ground, beyond a cat’s reach. its roof is painted green, and a clear side shows how much seed remains. the owner fills it in the morning while wearing red gloves.","the feeder was hidden behind thick branches. we moved it where birds could reach it. soon several birds began visiting each morning.","the fish flashed with a gray, metal-like shine; it looked ___.","the flock had twelve ___, all growing thick wool.","the flock held twenty woolly ___.","the footpath became slippery after rain.","the fox brushed snow from its fur. it followed tracks to a cabin, knocked politely, and asked the rabbit to vote for it as mayor.","the frog ___ over the log in one big spring.","the frog hid under the largest pond leaf.","the garden opens to visitors every june.","the garden path is twenty metres long. our neighbour calls it the prettiest path in town. i prefer its flowers to the ones by the gate.","the garden slept beneath the snow, one window shone with golden glow.","the garden swing goes up so high, my shoes point briefly at the sky. then down i swoop towards the ground, and hear the leaves make whispered sound.","the garden was dark. an owl hooted beyond the wall.","the gardener called the soil moist. it felt slightly wet between her fingers. it was neither dusty nor full of water. she said the seeds would grow well there. we gently covered each seed and labelled the row.","the gardener noticed deep cracks in the oak’s bark. glossary bark: the rough outer covering of a tree bark: the short loud sound a dog makes branch: a part growing out from a tree trunk","the gardener picked a ___ with five pink petals.","the gate blocks our way. opening it ___ our way.","the gate had been locked. dad turned the key and it could open.","the girls bag","the girls put on their coats. ___ went outside.","the girls’ bag","the glass mountain adventures beyond the valley cover art by rowan grey text by cleo west","the glue had dried our model was ready","the goalkeeper tipped the ball above the goal.","the group could not hear our spoken cue over the drums. we agreed on a hand signal. at the next rehearsal everyone stopped together.","the guide offered two routes from the visitor centre beside the lake. one followed a straight path to a village across the fields. the other route was circular, forming a loop around the water. walkers on that route passed the woods before reaching a small bridge. beyond it, a different path followed the opposite shore home. they finished at the visitor centre without retracing their outward steps. neither route climbed a hill or entered the nearby mountain area. the family chose the loop so their car would be waiting there.","the harbour was lively when the fishing boats returned each morning. engines hummed while workers called across the dock and carried boxes. buyers checked the catches, and drivers loaded vans for the market. by midnight, the same place was still and almost silent. the boxes remained stacked, but nobody moved among them then. boats rested at their ropes with their engines switched off. deep water lay beneath the dock at both times of day. at dawn, the returning crews brought movement and voices again.","the heavy load made her lose balance and take uneven steps. she ___ towards the bench.","the helper held the bag open while the cleaner swept dust into it.","the hidden gate by sam oak illustrated by kim lake","the hidden harbour a journey through caves written by remy woods island explorers","the hiker checked a ___ to find north.","the hill rose sharply, making the path ___.","the horse lifted both front ___ to clear the fence.","the hotel ___ cleaned the room and changed the sheets.","the hotel has twelve ___, each with a bed.","the hungry gull followed the fishing boat until it sailed away from the harbour.","the hungry puppy gobbled all of his dinner. he took four huge mouthfuls without pausing to chew. in moments, the food bowl was completely empty. then he searched its edges for one last crumb.","the ice became water in the warm room. it ___.","the icy handle felt rough. beyond the dark door, faint footsteps echoed down the hall.","the instructions say that water is needed only when the soil feels dry. add water ___ the soil feels dry.","the island has three sandy ___ beside the sea.","the jacket kept me warm during the cold wind. explain why.","the jar is ___ tight for me to open.","the jar of buttons ___ on the desk now.","the keeper fed the hungry penguins, so they were full before the first visitors arrived.","the kettle boiled dad made tea","the kettle bubbled gently. ping! the toast sprang up. ben scraped butter over it while a spoon clinked against his cup.","the kettle is full. ___ is heavy.","the kettle sends a cloud of steam, the morning makes the windows gleam. a butter knife beside my plate reminds my hungry hands to wait.","the kettle was hot. it gave a thin whistle.","the key you need has a round red tag.","the keyboard broke, so i had to ___ the note by hand.","the keys beside the bowl ___ missing now.","the kitchen door stood open. warm lamplight spilled onto the path, and friendly laughter floated out. three chairs stood around the square table.","the kite is red. the kite has a long tail.","the kitten is tame. the tiger is ___.","the kitten left the basket by the stairs and curled up behind the warm stove.","the kitten telling its own story","the kitten was found inside the tall cupboard.","the kittens followed their mother. ___ curled up together while their mother ate.","the kittens licked ___ own paws.","the knot would not come loose despite many tries; i felt ___.","the label says the cover can be washed without being damaged.","the lake was icy: its surface was ___.","the lamp ___ brightly every night.","the lane was chilly, meaning a little cold. pip pulled his sleeves down over his fingers. the morning air felt cold against his face. he welcomed the warmth when they reached the shop.","the lantern is blue. the lantern hangs beside the door.","the lantern tree written and illustrated by oona west cover lettering by miles brook for mum","the last bus arrived after dark.","the last runner crossed the line. everyone clapped.","the last trip of the year takes