sing ferry sent gentle waves towards its wooden hull. the boat bobbed as each wave reached the place it floated. its nose rose above the dock''s edge, then dropped below it. the next wave brought the same change in height again. its rope kept it near the post throughout this movement. it did not travel down the harbour or turn in circles. when the water settled, the boat''s nose stayed level beside the dock.","the locker you need is below the clock, with a blue star on its door.","the long way back illustrated by asha reed by felix green for aunt rosa, who showed us the way.","the longest river in this book is the nile.","the lost button pictures by tara west written by eli stone","the lost mitten lay beside a puddle.","the lost sock words: ruth cole art: max pine","the magician placed a bright coin on his open palm. everyone could see its silver edge under the stage lights. he closed both hands, clapped once and opened them again. the coin seemed to vanish while the audience was watching. he spread his fingers and slowly showed both empty palms. the children searched for a flash of silver but saw none. later, the coin appeared beneath a cup on the table. its size and colour were unchanged when a child examined it.","the map labels the large continent as africa.","the map showed large ___ connected by highways.","the market opens at seven in the morning.","the mechanic inspected the wheel. she turned it slowly, looked closely at each part and tested where the rubbing sound came from. only after these checks did she reach for a tool.","the medal was presented to ___ at the assembly.","the missing acorn story by beau reed illustrated by imogen lake series created by elio park","the moonlit fair stories after sunset illustrations by small lantern studio written by mina hart","the mouse crept ___, without making a sound.","the mouse was very small: it was ___.","the museum is in ___.","the museum takes care to protect its fragile objects. glass cases keep visitors from touching the old pottery. the entrance hall has six tall windows. low lighting helps stop delicate fabrics from fading. a café beside the exit sells fruit juice.","the musicians unpacked their instruments. one lifted a violin, another opened a flute case and a third set up a drum. soon their different sounds filled the room.","the narrow gap was too low to walk through, so i ___ beneath it on my hands and knees.","the neighbors lent us ___ ladder and later came to collect it.","the new bus was designed to help passengers travel comfortably. a low entrance allows easier boarding for people who cannot climb high steps. the bus is painted blue and white. clear screens show the next stop so passengers know when to get off. its route number is twelve.","the new door makes the reading room quieter. explain why.","the new path has a smooth surface and a gentle slope instead of steep steps. a wheelchair user can reach the hall along it. there are yellow flowers beside the path, and a notice records when the work was finished.","the new puppy chewed every shoe in the house while everyone was outside gardening.","the next sentences describe a bag’s pockets and strong handles.","the next sentences describe checking a map, packing water and choosing a safe meeting place.","the next sentences describe checking tools for damage and returning them to marked spaces after use.","the next sentences describe dot''s fins, eyes, and tail.","the next sentences describe what is kept in the garden shed.","the next sentences explain how the pool is cleaned and how swimmers are kept safe.","the next sentences explain how to care for a hamster.","the next sentences explain how worms loosen soil and mix dead leaves into it.","the next sentences explain rolling the die and moving a counter.","the next sentences explain that labels help us find supplies and put them back in the right place.","the next sentences explain that the shelter’s roof blocks rain and casts shade when the sun is strong.","the next sentences explain that we built a barrier near the deep water and added signs explaining safe routes.","the next sentences explain that we use both sides of paper and turn small scraps into labels.","the next sentences explain when the school bell rings.","the next sentences name places to change, shower and swim.","the next sentences tell how families repaired costumes and pupils practised the music for a play.","the next sentences tell how our class made a bird feeder.","the next sentences tell how to put on boots and a raincoat.","the next sentences tell how we learned new pupils’ names and invited them to join our games.","the next sentences tell where a bird found twigs and soft grass.","the note says our class visits on wednesday.","the note was addressed ___ the school cook.","the old box split under the books. as a result, we found a stronger one. the box split, ___ we replaced it.","the old game instructions filled four pages with repeated explanations. the club rewrote them before welcoming new players next week. their new instructions were concise, fitting neatly on one small card. a reader learned the goal and rules within half a minute. the card omitted stories about how the game had been invented. however, it kept the order of turns and how scoring worked. new players began correctly without needing another sheet or extra explanation. the longer version stayed in the cupboard, unused during their first game.","the old handle broke, and we fitted a ___ one.","the old sign used tiny pale letters. the replacement uses large dark letters on a light background, visible from the far gate. its wooden frame is older than the post. a gardener planted flowers below it after it was installed.","the old stairs were ___ and groaned under our feet.","the open book shows pages 4 and 5. you have finished both pages.","the opening was tiny and dark. i leaned close and looked carefully through it. i ___ inside.","the orange balloon floated.","the otter surface