ok another route.","the path was grey. gravel crunched beneath our boots.","the path was muddy, ___ we wore our boots to keep dry.","the path was narrow, with little space across it. we had to walk in a single line. two people could not stand side by side there. the next wide path gave everyone more room.","the path was too muddy for visitors. the park team covered it with a firm surface and added drainage along its edge. after rain, water could run away and visitors could use the path without sinking into mud.","the paths around the lake ___ at the gate.","the pencil was too ___ to reach the bottom of the jar.","the picnic was almost ready when large drops struck the blanket. a roofed shelter stood across the grass, some distance from their tree. everyone dashed towards it, carrying whatever food they could reach. their feet splashed through the shallow puddles forming on the path. they reached the roof breathing hard, before the cakes were soaked. nobody stopped to examine flowers or collect the scattered leaves. once under cover, they slowed down and put the food safely aside. the rain grew heavier while they looked back at the empty tree.","the picture of the horses ___ a wooden frame.","the picture was drawn by ___.","the pig is in the mud___","the pipe hummed behind the wall. a drop hung from the tap, then fell. plop! it landed in the bucket while water hissed through another pipe.","the plane landed in ___ after dark.","the plant began to wilt before we watered it. explain why.","the play’s opening was slow, but the actors made the forest scenes lively. a simple cloth became both a river and a waterfall. i would recommend the show to anyone who enjoys imaginative staging, though very young viewers may find it long.","the points won in a game","the puppet has long ears and a short tail, with one missing button eye.","the puppy nudged my knee with its soft nose. my leg moved a little from the gentle push. it did not bite or make any noise. i looked down to see 