nners lined up at the start. ___. finally, they crossed the finish line.","the sail lay low on the deck. two sailors pulled hard on the rope and hoisted it. up it rose along the tall pole until the wind filled it above their heads.","the sailor lowered an ___ to stop the boat drifting.","the school divided the pupils into four ___.","the school fixed dripping taps and collected rainwater for its garden. pupils also turned taps off while soaping their hands. each action reduced water that would otherwise be wasted. the school checked its use over time to see whether the changes helped.","the school garden provides places for wildlife to live. a pile of logs offers dark spaces for beetles. the gate was painted green last week. nest boxes give birds sheltered places to raise their young. the sign at the entrance carries the school’s name.","the school hall felt pleasantly warm after its heater started. the small office next door remained frigid throughout the morning. inside, the principal kept her coat buttoned beneath a thick blanket. even after rubbing her hands, her fingers felt painfully cold. she moved her work into the hall while waiting for repairs. both rooms had been quiet before the children arrived. the difference was not their noise or how neatly papers were arranged. warm air finally reached the office when its heater was fixed.","the school library opens at eight each morning. it closes at four in the afternoon. please return books at the desk.","the sea looked calm from the beach, but a sign warned against swimming.","the seam needed six more ___ to close the hole.","the season after winter","the sea’s level rises and falls along many coasts. at high tide, water covers parts of the shore that are exposed at low tide. tide tables help people find out when these changes are expected.","the seed has tiny hooks. during a walk, several seeds caught firmly in a dog’s fur and stayed there until it reached another field. the seed cases were brown, and the dog had walked past a pond.","the seed is smaller than a pea. it is ___.","the shed door had stood in rain for many years. its lower hinge was corroded, unlike the shiny new hinge above. orange flakes fell away when dad brushed the old metal gently. underneath, small holes had appeared where solid metal once joined. dad replaced it before the weak hinge could snap. the new hinge moved smoothly without losing flakes or powder. he added a protective coating to keep water from the metal. the old piece crumbled further when it was placed in a box.","the shelf was ___ high for me to reach.","the ship carried cargo, the goods being moved from one place to another. workers lifted boxes of fruit off the deck and loaded crates of tools for the next port.","the ship left the harbor for the open ___.","the shoes are wet. put ___ by the heater.","the shop hung two ___ on hangers.","the shop sold footwear for different days. boots waited near the door, sandals filled a summer shelf and trainers stood beside sports socks. customers tried them on their feet.","the shop was named after its owner, ___.","the short loud sound a dog makes","the sick rabbit was examined by a ___.","the sign allows just ___ person at a time.","the sky was bright ___ after the clouds cleared.","the small bells jingled as the band passed. boom! the largest drum answered. a whistle squealed, and the players began another tune.","the small bird made a nest.","the small boat floated beneath the wooden bridge___","the smallest star written and illustrated by farah lake published by night sky books for every dreamer","the smooth pebble shone.","the snail ___ slowly, leaving a silver line.","the snail slid along the leaf while an ant hurried past carrying a crumb.","the snow sparkled in the pale light. my fingers stung inside my gloves. each step made a crisp crunch as i crossed the frozen path.","the soup ___, making bubbles as it got very hot.","the soup was hot, so i took a tiny drink. i ___ it.","the soup was tasty, or ___.","the speaker asked all of us to raise ___ hands.","the stars shine at night___","the story has twelve chapters. to me, the final chapter is the funniest. our teacher thinks its cover is the most beautiful in the library.","the sunflower is taller than the rose bush.","the sunflower race story and pictures by milo ray a read-together book","the swans glided across the quiet blue lake. their bodies moved smoothly without making a splash. their feet paddled out of sight below the water. small ripples spread gently behind them as they passed.","the syrup held my fingers together; it felt ___.","the tall cup holds juice. the short cup holds water.","the team had a limited supply of string for its model. instead of using a whole length for each small join, asha measured. she cut just enough to hold each pair of sticks firmly. she saved the short pieces for tying the smallest parts together. by the end, her group still had string to spare. the teacher described their method as economical. another group had used twice as much for a similar model. asha showed them how the leftover pieces could still be useful.","the telephone lay beside amir’s notes. before calling the coach, he rehearsed his first sentence twice and twisted the cord around his finger. the number was already written at the top of the page.","the tennis match ended when the last point was won. glossary match: a small stick used to start a flame match: a contest between players or teams score: the points won in a game","the thick main stem of a tree","the three ___ wag their tails.","the time when daylight fades","the time when daylight first appears","the tiny door story: sana bell art: evan cole","the tiny print looked larger through the ___.","the tiny print was hard to see in the dim room. ava leaned close and peered at the label. she narrowed her eyes until she could make out the small letters.","the towel was no longer dripping, but it was still slightly wet, or ___.","the towel was slightly wet, but not dripping; it was ___.","the towel was soaked. its opposite is completely ___.","the towels felt fluffy and smelled of soap. sunlight lit their white edges. beside them, the washing machine hummed through its final cycle.","the tower rose high above the square. its bells rang loudly.","the toy car track should start on a ramp.","the train rolled along two metal ___.","the tree","the twins ___ over the puddle.","the twins labelled both bags with ___ names.","the twins packed ___ bags for camp.","the twins painted their bedroom door bright orange.","the twins tested their puppet. “i will move the arms,” said ada. “then i will move the head,” replied elle. they ducked behind the screen to practise.","the twins thanked their uncle after he repaired their bicycle beside the old garden shed.","the twins visited auntie vee on sunday, and she taught them a new game.","the twins’ tent wasn’t empty.","the two ___ meet in different rooms.","the two cloths behaved differently when we spilled water. one was absorbent, soaking up the puddle until the table dried. the other let the drops stay on top and roll off. we pressed each cloth with the same amount of force. then we weighed them to find how much water they held. the absorbent cloth was much heavier after the test. we chose it for cleaning the painting tables at school. the other cloth became a cover to protect a tray.","the two kittens ___ beside the fire now.","the two newborn ___ slept in separate cribs.","the unopened packet contained a ___ toothbrush.","the vase was fragile, or easy to break. mom held it carefully with both her hands. she kept it away from the table''s edge. a small knock could crack its thin glass sides.","the waiter carried six plates on one arm.","the walkers reached the hut after carrying bags uphill all afternoon. they were weary, worn out by the steep final climb. their usual lively conversation had stopped before the last bend. at the door, they lowered their bags and sat without sp