tified by this cover.","Imogen Lake is the picture maker identified by this cover.","Impossible. Which letter matches the first sound?","In A, I is inside Zed’s speech; in B it is the narrator’s voice.","In early spring, small leaves opened on the branch. During summer they spread wide. In autumn their colour changed, and later they fell. By winter the same branch was bare.","In fall, the tree shed many brown ___.","In spring, new leaves opened on the bare branches.","In spring, new leaves opened on the bare branches.\nGlossary\nspring: the season after winter\nspring: a curled piece of metal that pushes back\nbud: a small new growth on a plant","In the community garden, everyone uses the same path and tool shed. A clear sign explains where tools belong. Gardeners return equipment clean and keep their plants from blocking the path. These small agreements help different people work comfortably in one place.","In the garden we planted beans peas and, carrots.","In the garden we planted beans, peas, and carrots.","In the garden we planted, beans peas and carrots.","In the story, a ___ worked in the queen’s household.","In the story, a … worked in the queen’s household. Which spelling fits?","In the story, the palace ___ was a woman who cleaned.","In the workshop, sharp tools go into covered holders. Heavy boxes stay on low shelves. Spilled liquid is wiped up quickly, and walking paths are kept clear. Each arrangement reduces a different way someone could be hurt.","Includes attribution and excludes some actual spoken words.","Includes the narrator’s attribution inside the quotation.","Includes the narrator’s attribution inside the spoken quotation.","Increase makes an amount larger; decrease and lessen both reduce it.","India","Ink. Choose the missing letters.","Ink. Which letter matches the first sound?","Ink. Which word has the same starting sound?","Insect. Which letter matches the first sound?","Insects visit its open flowers. does not satisfy the complete evidence. Reduced water loss directly supports saving water; the flower facts concern pollination.","Insects visit its open flowers.","Inside Niko’s teacup, a tiny sea began to roar. A little ship sailed up to the rim and asked for sugar.","Inside a Seed","Inside the family den","Inside the family den, page 22","Inside the house, Sol slept through the storm. Outside, a fox crept past his window. Sol never knew how close it had come to the glass.","Inside the parcel was ___ tiny wooden boat.","Inside the parcel was a tiny wooden boat. Build the missing word.","Inside. Which word has the same starting sound?","Instead of crossing the bridge, the goat stepped carefully along stones through the shallow stream.","Insufficient reach concerns length; width and weight do not explain it.","Insulation explains warmth, while the ticket and zipper detail do not.","Integrate a linked explanation across three facts; distinguish related duck topics.","Interpret a bare byline among separate map and illustration credits.","Interprets figurative comparison as literal light production.","Interprets human-like description as literal speech.","Interprets the cloud comparison as literal location.","Introduces a past sighting rather than general care needs.","Introduces appearance rather than how to care for a hamster.","Introduces feeding rather than the appearance described next.","Introduces places to ride rather than safety actions.","Introduces plants’ growing needs rather than pollen movement.","Introduces the fish’s purchase rather than its appearance.","Invents a narrator absent from the text.","Invents a person despite the explicit absence of speech.","Invents a person despite the explicit information.","Invents an adult narrator absent from the text.","Invents the kitten as narrator without first-person evidence.","Iris Lake is the picture maker identified by this cover.","Iris","Is ___ in our group?","Is anybody ___?","Is the bug on the rug?","Is the bug on the rug___","Is the door open!","Is the door open.","Is the door open?","Is the door open___","Is the soup still hot!","Is the soup still hot.","Is the soup still hot?","Is this ___ scarf or yours?","Island Explorers identifies a different printed role or position. The Hidden Harbour is the title identified by this cover.","Isolate the final phoneme from the /nd/ consonant cluster rather than a simple final consonant.","Isolate the final phoneme from the /st/ consonant cluster against an internal-sound competitor.","It ___ thunder later.","It addresses paper and handling, not paint selection.","It asks no pet-care questions.","It assigns fantasy work to a giraffe instead of describing its diet.","It can ___ windy up here.","It carried a crumb.: Sliding is the snail’s action; the other actions belong to the ant.","It concerns a living plant, not a toy sale.","It crossed the bridge.: The goat used stepping stones; the sentence explicitly excludes the bridge and describes shallow water.","It does not list tools or materials.","It does not narrate an individual character’s visit.","It does not report real animal information.","It does not satisfy the complete evidence. They refers to the kittens; their mother is the separate singular animal.","It does not satisfy the complete evidence. They refers to the plural girls.","It explains using counters, not making them.","It gives explanations rather than planting directions.","It happened long ago.: Untrue means not true; being long ago does not make a story false.","It has a paper hat.","It held twelve coins, while the first held only four.","It hurried past the snail.: Sliding is the snail’s action; the other actions belong to the ant.","It is ___ to pack away.","It is a new rule.: Un means not in unfair; age of the rule is unrelated.","It is always fair.: Un means not in unfair; age of the rule is unrelated.","It is cold ___ ice.","It is dark. Please turn ___ the lamp.","It is more fun to play with ice than with sand.","It is not a factual account o