d?","Planets","Plant adds a final /t/ that was not spoken.","Plant. Choose the missing letters.","Planting followed the frost and preceded harvest; the other times conflict with the sequence.","Plate. Which printed word matches the recording?","Play comes immediately after dogs when reading from left to right.","Play follows dogs in left-to-right reading.","Play your ___ in the show.","Play. Which letters complete the word?","Playful describes readiness for play, not sleep or concealment.","Please ___ a boat on the paper.","Please ___ a clean cloth.","Please ___ beside your partner.","Please ___ both hands to carry it.","Please ___ inside the empty box.","Please ___ inside; we are waiting for you.","Please ___ my hat. I lost it.","Please ___ quiet during the story.","Please ___ quiet while the baby sleeps.","Please ___ still on this chair.","Please ___ the buckle before the ride begins.","Please ___ the date at the top.","Please ___ the door quietly.","Please ___ the pencil back to me.","Please ___ the soup with care.","Please ___ the switch once.","Please ___ through the open gate.","Please ___ your nose using a tissue.","Please and the request to use a bin show the writer’s purpose.","Please ask ben to help.","Please bring one clean cardboard tube tomorrow.","Please bring the empty basket from the kitchen.","Please carry this bowl.","Please close ___ little gate.","Please close the gate and lock it behind you. does not satisfy the complete evidence. The first sign satisfies both closing and not locking.","Please close the little gate. Listen. Choose its missing word.","Please close the window\nbefore rain comes in.","Please come invites the family to attend the performance.","Please come through the open gate. Listen. Pick the missing word.","Please feed the cat tomorrow and keep it indoors. does not satisfy the complete evidence. The first request keeps both the time and the indoor condition.","Please feed the cat tonight and let it outside. does not satisfy the 