tisfy the complete evidence. Only the first request identifies the scarf using the supplied details.","Please pass the blue cup with a white stripe on its handle. does not satisfy the complete evidence. The inside-rim detail distinguishes this cup from the other blue cups.","Please pass the empty bowl.","Please pour a little ___ juice.","Please pour a little more juice. Listen. Pick the missing word.","Please put ___ cup on the tray.","Please put my shoes in the box. does not satisfy the complete evidence. The first request asks for the specified help.","Please put your boots here.","Please put your cup on the tray. Listen. Pick the missing word.","Please save a slice of cake ___ our neighbour.","Please save a slice of cake for our neighbour. Build the missing word.","Please sit beside your partner. Listen. Pick the missing word.","Please take your bag when you leave. does not satisfy the complete evidence. Only the first sign requests wiping feet.","Please use both hands to carry it. Listen. Pick the missing word.","Please wait here. I will fetch the key.","Please water my plant tomorrow. does not satisfy the complete evidence. Only the first message thanks the neighbour for what she did.","Please write the date at the top. Listen. Pick the missing word.","Please … quiet while the baby sleeps. Which spelling fits?","Please … the buckle before the ride begins. Which word fits?","Plink imitates the light metallic sound.","Plink","Plop imitates the single drop’s landing.","Plop","Plug. Choose the missing letters.","Plug. Which printed word matches the recording?","Plug. Which vowel completes the word?","Plum. Which letter spells the middle vowel sound?","Plums","Plural birds takes are; the singular roof is only a location.","Plural ducks agrees with are for what is happening now.","Plural geese takes are, not is or am.","Plural roots controls take; the nearby singular tree does not control the verb.","Pocket depth concerns storage.","Pocket. Choose the missing letters.","Pole. Which vowel pattern completes the word?","Police caught two ___ who had stolen the bicycles.","Pond and bed end in /d/. Pen ends in /n/; dog starts with /d/ but ends in /g/.","Pond names the place.","Pond, desert and forest are living places; the final sentence confirms that relation.","Pond. Choose the missing letters.","Pond. Put the sounds in order to make the word.","Pond. Which letters complete the ending?","Ponies are small equines ridden in paddocks; pony is singular and puppies cannot carry riders.","Pop imitates the sudden noise of the bursting balloon.","Pop the coins ___ the tin.","Pop","Pop. Which word rhymes with it?","Poppy","Porch. Which letters complete the word?","Porous material admits water through holes; solid and waterproof do not explain absorption.","Position by a window is not itself evidence of growth.","Postage is paid with stamps; stamp names one and buttons do not pay postage.","Posting connects writing with later delivery.","Pot. Which letter matches the final sound?","Pot. Which letter matches the first sound?","Pot. Which printed word matches the recording?","Pot. Which vowel completes the word?","Potatoes are vegetables peeled for soup; potato names one and plates cannot be peeled as food.","Pots cooking identify the kitchen; the other rooms serve different uses.","Pour milk ___ the jug until it fills.","Pour the clean water ___ this narrow-necked bottle carefully.","Pour the clean water into this narrow-necked bottle carefully. Build the missing word.","Pour the mixture through the ___ so the liquid passes but the lumps stay.","Precut marks cutting in advance; recut means again and cutting marks ongoing action.","Predicting states an expected future result; preventing stops something from happening and repeating says something again.","Preparation includes all three actions, rather than only route-finding.","Prepay means pay beforehand; repay means pay back and paying marks ongoing action.","Press the bell before your stop.","Press the lemon halves firmly to ___ out the juice.","Press the lemon halves firmly to … out the juice. Which word fits?","Press the sticky flap down to seal the envelope.","Press the sticky flap down to seal the envelope.\nGlossary\nseal: a sea animal with flippers\nseal: to close something tightly\nstamp: a small payment label for a letter","Prettiest is a preference, not a measurement.","Prewash marks washing beforehand; rewash means again and washed marks past action.","Pride fits satisfaction in one’s own effort; shame and jealousy have different causes.","Print. Choose the missing letters.","Printing processes are not described.","Priya left home without a coat because the sky was clear. Halfway back from the shop, a sudden shower reached her street. She arrived drenched, with her clothes soaked right through. Water dripped from her sleeves even after she squeezed them out. Her shopping stayed dry inside its closed waterproof bag. Priya changed every wet layer before sitting beside the warm heater. The towel she used for her hair quickly became wet too. Only the things protected inside the bag escaped the shower.","Prize. Which vowel pattern completes the word?","Prompt returns help other borrowers.","Protecting Food on a Journey","Protection from rain is the shared topic, not keeping cool.","Protective quills distinguish a porcupine from these other furry mammals.","Prune. Which vowel pattern completes the word?","Pull the rope ___ until the little flag reaches the top.","Pull the rope up until the little flag reaches the top. Build the missing word.","Pulling apart with a ragged edge is tearing, not bending or flattening.","Pumpkin. Which letter matches the first sound?","Pup. Which word rhymes with it?","Pupils choose different games to play after lunch.","Pupils collect playground litter.","Pupils keep coats on their named hooks indoors.","Purple is the loveliest colour.","Purple. Which letters complete the word?","Purr imitates the low, steady noise the cat makes.","Purr! The cat curled up on my lap. Its eyes slowly closed.","Purr","Purse. Which letters spell the vowel sound in this word?","Push off hard and ___ across the wide ditch.","Push off hard and … across the wide ditch. Which word fits?","Push the string through the bead to ___ it.","Push the string through the bead to … it. Which word fits?","Put /s/ before top without changing the other sounds: stop.","Put a seed in soil. Add water. Leave the pot near light.","Put all the red counters together to ___ them by color.","Put all the red counters together to … them by color. Which word fits?","Put each block directly on the one below to ___ them.","Put each block directly on the one below to … them. Which word fits?","Put the dry leaves here.","Put your empty plate over ___.","Put your empty plate over there. Listen. Pick the missing word.","Put your shoes on your feet. does not satisfy the complete evidence. The socks must go on before the shoes.","Put","Puts a capital inside the day name.","Puts a comma between the subject and verb.","Puts a comma between the verb and its first object.","Puts only part of the speech and some attribution inside the marks.","Puts the apostrophe after an added s instead of after the girl’s name.","Puts the capital at the end rather than the beginning.","Putting away a bag is an ordinary action that does not establish relief.","Putting on a hat made sweets fall from the sky.","Putting the letter inside must precede sealing; the sealed envelope can then be posted.","Putting tools back helps the next person find them quickly.","Quack imitates the duck, while the other noises have different sources.","Quack","Quiet and wake do not rhyme.","Quietness is not the shared purpose of the changes.","Quilt. Choose the missing letters.","Quotation marks, comma and full stop attach to words; the five words are Please, wait, called, Mr and Fox.","Quoted speech in A is not the surrounding narrative voice.","Rabbit. Which letter matches the 