 a class as the credited writer rather than assuming an individual name must be correct.","Recognize a question as the book title while distinguishing words and drawings credits.","Recognize a question title against a descriptive subtitle and an art studio name.","Recognize an art studio as the credited illustrator rather than choosing a person name.","Recognize an invitation among a question and a request.","Recognize that one person can write the story and make its pictures.","Recognize the artist in a combined writing-and-drawing credit.","Recording growth directly supports learning by observation.","Red Oak Press identifies a different printed role or position. Home at Last! is the title identified by this cover.","Red tells its colour.","Red, yellow and blue stripes made the scarf ___.","Red, yellow and blue stripes made the scarf …. Which word fits?","Red. Which word rhymes with it?","Reduced water loss directly supports saving water; the flower facts concern pollination.","Reducing noise supports the claim about concentration.","Refill repeats filling; the alternatives do not replace its contents.","Refuse declines what accepting allows; agree and receive relate to acceptance.","Rehearsal helps us sing together.","Reheated means heated again; preheated is before use and unheated means not heated.","Relaxing and a peaceful sigh directly show calmness.","Relaxing and releasing breath show the feeling; finding his brother explains its cause.","Relaxing describes the narrator’s experience.","Relieved describes worry ending when the puppy is safe.","Removes the useful information rather than clarifying it.","Removing /s/ leaves the spoken word no.","Removing man from snowman leaves snow.","Removing only the initial phoneme from clap leaves lap.","Removing only the initial phoneme from glow leaves low.","Removing only the initial phoneme from slip leaves lip.","Removing only the initial phoneme from smile leaves mile.","Removing only the initial phoneme from spot leaves pot.","Removing only the initial phoneme from stack leaves tack.","Removing only the initial phoneme from stop leaves top.","Removing only the initial phoneme from train leaves rain.","Removing the whole word part bed from bedroom leaves room.","Removing the whole word part coat from raincoat leaves rain.","Removing the whole word part pack from backpack leaves back.","Removing the whole word part sea from seashell leaves shell.","Removing the whole word part sun from sunset leaves set.","Removing tooth from toothbrush leaves brush.","Remy Woods","Reopen reverses a closure by opening again; it does not mean moving.","Reorders the original sounds while adding /s/.","Repaint repeats painting; removing or opening does not change paint.","Repairing a discarded drawer illustrates useful reuse.","Repairing a tooth is a dentist’s work; the other occupations do not match the dental clue.","Repairing books would preserve our stories and save money.","Repeated rehearsal and restless handling of the cord suggest tension before the call.","Repeated unsuccessful effort produces frustration; content and amused do not describe that obstacle.","Repeating the instruction supplies the missing information.","Repeats the proposed change without explaining its benefit.","Repeats the proposed plan without giving a reason for it.","Replace only the first sound: pan becomes fan.","Replaces movement with rest.","Replaces one quick jump with unhurried movement.","Replaces the cluster with a new consonant instead of deleting only /s/.","Replaces the first phoneme while keeping the rime.","Replacing a broken part repairs the cart; decorating or borrowing does not restore it.","Replacing only the final phoneme of bag with the last sound of sun makes ban.","Replacing only the final phoneme of bed with the last sound of hat makes bet.","Replacing only the final phoneme of cat with the last sound of cup makes cap.","Replacing only the final phoneme of cup with the last sound of hat makes cut