nd stopped to collect passengers. The driver steered while we sat together.\nText B: I cycled to school with Dad. We chose the quiet streets and stopped when we needed a rest.","Text A: Our library lends books and provides tables where visitors can study. Staff help people find what they need.\nText B: The mobile library lends books from a van. It visits villages that are far from a library building.","Text A: Our team crowded around the notice. We had won the photo competition!\nText B: The team crowded around the notice and discovered that it had won the photo competition.","Text A: The hikers slept in a fabric tent that folded into a bag. They carried it to the next campsite.\nText B: The stone shelter stayed beside the mountain path. Travellers could rest there, but could not take it away.","Text A: The market was quiet before sunrise. Sellers arranged fruit while only a few early shoppers passed.\nText B: By late morning, the same market was crowded. Shoppers queued and sellers called across the busy stalls.","Text A: The sailors hauled the small boat onto the beach before the waves grew higher.\nText B: We hauled our boat onto the beach just before the next wave reached us.","Text A: We covered young plants with a mesh frame to keep birds from eating the leaves. Rain could pass through the mesh.\nText B: The gardener used shiny hanging strips to discourage birds from landing among the seedlings.","Text A: We pushed our boat into the water.\nText B: The children pushed their boat into the water.","Text A: We walked through the museum together and stopped at the giant skeleton.\nText B: The class walked through the museum and stopped at the giant skeleton.","Text A: “I cannot reach,” said Zed, stretching towards the shelf.\nText B: I stretched towards the shelf but could not reach the book.","Text B explicitly refers to the same market.","Thank you for fixing my bike. I will ride it home tonight. does not satisfy the complete evidence. The first message thanks A