he jug. We put … into the cupboard, but left the jug out.","The box colour does not show care.","The box had a red handle.","The box held buttons ribbons and, beads.","The box held buttons, ribbons, and beads.","The box held keepsakes from our seaside trip. There was a ticket, postcard, and tiny shell. Each object helped us remember a special day. We showed them while telling friends about our holiday.","The box held, buttons ribbons and beads.","The box is big. The bag is ___ big.","The box is full ___ toys.","The box of coloured pencils ___ on the shelf now.","The box of coloured pencils … on the shelf now.","The box of costumes belongs to ___.","The box was brown.","The boy fastened ___ helmet.","The boy fastened his helmet. Listen. Pick the missing word.","The boy kicked the ball. It went into the goal. Then his team cheered. What happened in the middle?","The boy loosened the knot and opened his parcel.","The boy rolled a large snowball. He added a smaller one for the head. Then he gave the snowman a hat. What happened last?","The boys have a ball. ___ play outside.","The boys have a ball. … play outside.","The boys watched their sister perform. ___ clapped when she finished.","The boys watched their sister perform. … clapped when she finished.","The brass trumpet gleamed. A loud note filled the hall.","The bread ___ rise by noon.","The breeze is the stated cause, not a person asking a question.","The breeze moved the leaves in lively, turning ways.","The bridge goes ___ the stream.","The bridge is a location, and its builder is not the narrator.","The bridge must be built before it can be load-tested.","The bridge test must happen only when the glue is dry. Test the bridge ___ the glue is completely dry.","The bridge test must happen only when the glue is dry. Test the bridge … the glue is completely dry.","The broad surface pushes against the water.","The broken wheel is the problem causing the feeling.","The broom woke up and swept the room by itself. Dust g