he captain said these words: Everyone is on board.","The captain said, “Everyone is on board.”","The captain “said, Everyone is on board.”","The captain’s cap had a silver badge.","The card contained good ___ for the coming year.","The card must be written before it can be sealed away and posted.","The card shows 8. Write the number word: ___.","The cardboard castle was made ___ the youngest children.","The cardboard castle was made by the youngest children. Build the missing word.","The careful looking, testing and checking show what inspected means.","The caretaker put up the signs during the holiday.","The carpenter cut a plank from solid ___.","The carpenter fitted two ___ for our books.","The carpenter sanded a rough piece of ___.","The carpenter sanded a rough piece of …. Which spelling fits?","The carrots, onions, beans and water are the things combined to make the soup.","The cart grew a shell.","The cart moved very slowly.","The cart slid without using its wheels.","The cases prevent handling damage, and low light reduces fading.","The case’s colour does not create urgency.","The castle had a stone window.","The castle shrank.","The cat jumped onto the box. Then it curled into a ball. Last, it fell asleep. What happened first?","The caterpillar ___ changed since we first brought it inside.","The caterpillar has changed since we first brought it inside. Build the missing word.","The chain squeaked until Dad added ___.","The chairs in our library have padded feet.","The chairs stand ___ one another.","The chapter total can be counted.","The chef laid five ___ by the plates.","The chick climbed ___ of its shell.","The chick climbed out of its shell. Listen. Pick the missing word.","The chicks? Feed ___ at five.","The child ___ found the wallet returned it to the teacher.","The child ___ the quiet part again so everyone could hear.","The child found some paper. She folded it into a plane. Then she flew it across the room. What happened last?","The child said the quiet part again so everyone could hear. Build the missing word.","The child said these words: May I borrow a ruler?","The child said, “May I borrow a ruler?”","The child walked over ___ the teacher and asked politely.","The child walked over to the teacher and asked politely. Build the missing word.","The child went up the rope by pulling with both hands and pushing with both feet.","The child who found the wallet returned it to the teacher. Build the missing word.","The child “said, May I borrow a ruler?”","The children ___ a snowman from three balls.","The children ___ on the mat for story time.","The children are passengers in her account.","The children beside the teacher ___ ready now.","The children beside the teacher … ready now.","The children carried water as they ran.","The children enjoy eating lunch together.","The children gave their teacher some flowers, and she placed them beside the classroom window.","The children hung up ___ coats.","The children hung up their coats. Listen. Pick the missing word.","The children lost their tickets, but someone returned ___ safely.","The children lost their tickets, but someone returned them safely. Build the missing word.","The children must wait outside the locked gate until an adult opens it for them.","The children outside after the rain. does not satisfy the complete evidence. The first choice contains a complete main clause after the time clause.","The children stand ___ each other.","The children washed clay from their hands in a basin, a wide bowl that held warm water. They dipped their fingers below the surface and rubbed off the mud.","The children will meet after lunch, although their teacher arrives before lunch.","The choir practices in the hall every Tuesday.","The class counted vehicles passing the school. A bus stopped, two bicycles rolled past and a delivery van turned the corner. Each carried someone or something along the road.","The class drawers should all have labels on them.","The class dug