r and farms beyond the distant trees. Nobody exchanged money, and the lookout had no ticket office. The tired walkers stayed much longer than they had planned. On the way down, they described their favourite parts of the view. Each agreed that reaching the top had been worth the climb.","The climbers could see everest from their camp.","The clock hangs ___ the wall.","The clock makes no sound. It is ___.","The clock makes no sound. It is ….","The clock shows the ___: three o''clock.","The clock struck ___ times at that hour.","The clock struck six as Ravi dropped his cup. He whispered a spell to the clock. Its hands spun backwards, the pieces joined together, and the cup jumped safely into his hand.","The clock struck six.","The clock struck … times at that hour. Which spelling fits?","The clock watched people with real eyes.","The clock’s position is neutral.","The cloth was a vivid, bright red called ___.","The cloth was a vivid, bright red called …. Which word fits?","The cloth was absorbent; it soaked up spilled water. The wet patch became smaller as we wiped. Soon, the table was dry and the cloth heavy. We squeezed the water out over the sink.","The clouds are dark, so it ___ rain before we arrive.","The clouds are dark, so it may rain before we arrive. Build the missing word.","The coach asked whether i had brought my hat.","The coach called my sister and me. She wanted to speak to ___.","The coach called my sister and me. She wanted to speak to ….","The coat goes on before its zip can be closed.","The coat has a smooth blue outer layer. Water forms drops on that layer and rolls away without soaking through. There are two deep pockets, and a yellow loop lets the coat hang on a hook.","The coat has two deep pockets.","The coat kept me dry but did not keep me warm. I stayed dry, ___ I still felt cold.","The coat kept me dry but did not keep me warm. I stayed dry, … I still felt cold.","The coats are kept on hooks during the school day.","The cockpit and airplane