ressed ___ the school cook.","The note was addressed … the school cook. Which spelling fits?","The notice gives closure dates and alternative access.","The notice offers help but does not provide every repair procedure.","The notice reports a found item and the collection place.","The number of branches can be checked by observation.","The number of chairs does not indicate sound level.","The number of colours used can be checked.","The observed test result is factual evidence.","The obstruction explains why the bus could not continue.","The office closes after the staff put away their work.","The office receives parcels from several delivery companies.","The oil keeps feathers dry, and the trapped air keeps the body warm.","The old box split under the books. As a result, we found a stronger one. The box split, ___ we replaced it.","The old box split under the books. As a result, we found a stronger one. The box split, … we replaced it.","The old game instructions filled four pages with repeated explanations. The club rewrote them before welcoming new players next week. Their new instructions were concise, fitting neatly on one small card. A reader learned the goal and rules within half a minute. The card omitted stories about how the game had been invented. However, it kept the order of turns and how scoring worked. New players began correctly without needing another sheet or extra explanation. The longer version stayed in the cupboard, unused during their first game.","The old handle broke, and we fitted a ___ one.","The old handle broke, and we fitted a … one. Which spelling fits?","The old sign used tiny pale letters. The replacement uses large dark letters on a light background, visible from the far gate. Its wooden frame is older than the post. A gardener planted flowers below it after it was installed.","The old stairs were ___ and groaned under our feet.","The open book shows pages 4 and 5.\nYou have finished both pages.","The opening captures the different 