g lunch.","The room was light. At bedtime it became ___.","The room was noisy, so Mia did not call across it. She beckoned to her friend, curling her fingers toward herself. Her friend saw the signal and came over.","The root entry says that roots take in water.","The roots grew longer when we gave the plant water!","The roots grew longer when we gave the plant water.","The roots grew longer when we gave the plant water?","The roots grew longer when we gave the plant water___","The roots have been planted and watered.","The roots of the tree ___ water from the soil.","The roots of the tree take water from the soil.","The roots of the tree takes water from the soil.","The roots of the tree taking water from the soil.","The rope colour is unchanged and does not explain the difference.","The rope explains attachment rather than calmness.","The rope was ___ enough.","The rope was blue in both trials.","The rope was long enough. Listen. Pick the missing word.","The rose bush is shorter than the sunflower.","The rose danced down the road.","The route number is twelve.","The route stayed the same.","The row and side together identify the seats.","The rubber band ___ longer as we pulled it.","The rubber strip bent easily without breaking; it was ___.","The rubber strip bent easily without breaking; it was …. Which word fits?","The rule allows entry only after the green light comes on. Wait here ___ the green light comes on.","The rule allows entry only after the green light comes on. Wait here … the green light comes on.","The rule applies before handling food regardless of visible dirt.","The runner heard the signal. She ran to the cone. Then she touched it. What happened first?","The runners collected ___ medals after the race.","The runners collected medals after the race.","The runners collected … medals after the race. Which spelling fits?","The runners lined up at the start. ___. Finally, they crossed the finish line.","The runners put on their shoes before lining up.","The sail lay low on the deck. Two sailors pulled hard on the rope and hoisted it. Up it rose along the tall pole until the wind filled it above their heads.","The sail rises as the sailors pull, establishing upward lifting.","The sailor lowered an ___ to stop the boat drifting.","The sailor lowered an … to stop the boat drifting. Which word fits?","The sailor untied the rope. She pushed the boat from the bank. Then she began rowing. What happened in the middle?","The scarf was wrapped around the cup; paper belongs to the other box.","The school bell’s ring carried across the field.: Silver and a gift box identify jewelry; bells and telephones identify sounds.","The school divided the pupils into four ___.","The school fixed dripping taps and collected rainwater for its garden. Pupils also turned taps off while soaping their hands. Each action reduced water that would otherwise be wasted. The school checked its use over time to see whether the changes helped.","The school garden provides places for wildlife to live. A pile of logs offers dark spaces for beetles. The gate was painted green last week. Nest boxes give birds sheltered places to raise their young. The sign at the entrance carries the school’s name.","The school hall felt pleasantly warm after its heater started. The small office next door remained frigid throughout the morning. Inside, the principal kept her coat buttoned beneath a thick blanket. Even after rubbing her hands, her fingers felt painfully cold. She moved her work into the hall while waiting for repairs. Both rooms had been quiet before the children arrived. The difference was not their noise or how neatly papers were arranged. Warm air finally reached the office when its heater was fixed.","The school has a tap beside the back door.","The school library opens at eight each morning. It closes at four in the afternoon. Please return books at the desk.","The sea looked calm from the beach, but a sign warned against swimming.","The seam needed six more ___ to close the hole.","The seasonal order shows changes in the same branch.","The sea’s level rises and falls along many coasts. At high tide, water covers parts of the shore that are exposed at low tide. Tide tables help people find out when these changes are expected.","The second sentence continues Jay’s speaking turn.","The second sentence shifts to completed past wrote.","The seed cases were brown.","The seed has tiny hooks. During a walk, several seeds caught firmly in a dog’s fur and stayed there until it reached another field. The seed cases were brown, and the dog had walked past a pond.","The seed is smaller than a pea. It is ___.","The seed is smaller than a pea. It is …. Which word fits?","The seedlings received the same watering throughout.","The seeds have no speech or fantasy actions.","The seeds went ___ the soil.","The seeds were carried to a new place on the animal.","The sentence changes from a usual present action to one past event.","The sentence explains the bowl’s benefit to birds.","The sentence gives a benefit rather than repeating the opinion.","The sentence gives a factual description of ice.","The sentence reports the child’s new achievement.","The sentence reports the completed planting.","The sentence reports the event that happened.","The sentence uses bank to mean a place that keeps and lends money; its actions and objects support that sense.","The sentence uses bark to mean the rough outer covering of a tree; its actions and objects support that sense.","The sentence uses jam to mean a blockage that stops movement; its actions and objects support that sense.","The sentence uses light to mean not heavy; its actions and objects support that sense.","The sentence uses match to mean a contest between players or teams; its actions and objects support that sense.","The sentence uses seal to mean to close something tightly; its actions and objects support that sense.","The sentence uses spring to mean the season after winter; i